    "conclusions": [
      "The read rate rises with radius, as constant angular velocity predicts: 1251.6 KiB/s at FAD 45150 to 2003.2 at 450000 (60% faster; mean of two runs). Every earlier optical figure in this project was the innermost, slowest point.",
      "The time spent in the long poll calls (the PIO transfers) is nearly constant across the radius (1424 ms at FAD 45150, 1368 ms at 450000, per 4.8 MB): PIO transfer costs the CPU about the same per byte wherever the head is.",
